### TalkBack API - Phase 1 Test Requests
### Use with REST Client extension in VS Code/Cursor

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@artifactId = <replace-with-actual-artifact-id>

### Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Database Ping
GET {{baseUrl}}/db/ping

### Create Artifact
POST {{baseUrl}}/artifacts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My First Artifact",
  "description": "This is a test artifact for Phase 1"
}

### Get Artifact (replace {id} with actual artifact ID from create response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/artifacts/{{artifactId}}

### Upload Material (multipart/form-data)
### Replace {id} with actual artifact ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/artifacts/{{artifactId}}/materials
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

This is a test file content.
It will be extracted as text since it's text/plain.
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="kind"

document
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--

### Upload Material with slides kind
POST {{baseUrl}}/artifacts/{{artifactId}}/materials
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="presentation.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./path/to/your/file.pdf
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="kind"

slides
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--

### Attach Video URL (Embed Mode - Backward Compatible)
POST {{baseUrl}}/artifacts/{{artifactId}}/video
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "provider": "loom",
  "video_url": "https://www.loom.com/share/example-video-id"
}

### Attach Video URL (Embed Mode - New Format)
POST {{baseUrl}}/artifacts/{{artifactId}}/video
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "provider": "loom",
  "playback_mode": "embed",
  "embed_url": "https://www.loom.com/share/example-video-id"
}

### Attach Video URL (Direct MP4 Mode)
POST {{baseUrl}}/artifacts/{{artifactId}}/video
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "provider": "other",
  "playback_mode": "direct",
  "media_url": "https://example.com/video.mp4",
  "poster_url": "https://example.com/poster.jpg",
  "duration_seconds": 1234
}

### Upload Transcript (replace {video_id} with actual video source ID from video response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/artifacts/{{artifactId}}/video/<video-id>/transcript
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transcript_text": "This is a sample transcript. It contains the full text of the video. In Phase 1, we store this directly without embeddings."
}

### Get Artifact with all materials and video sources
GET {{baseUrl}}/artifacts/{{artifactId}}

### Get Artifact with questions included
GET {{baseUrl}}/artifacts/{{artifactId}}?include_questions=true

### Phase 2: Ask a Question
POST {{baseUrl}}/artifacts/{{artifactId}}/questions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question_text": "What is the main topic discussed in this artifact?"
}

### Phase 2: Get Questions for an Artifact (returns recent questions with their latest answers)
GET {{baseUrl}}/artifacts/{{artifactId}}/questions

### Phase 2: Ask a Question (should return not_covered if content doesn't exist)
POST {{baseUrl}}/artifacts/{{artifactId}}/questions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question_text": "What is the weather like today?"
}

### Phase 3: Sessions

### Create Session (independent - no artifact required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Weekly review - Jan 2026",
  "created_by": "Paresh"
}

### Get Session Details
@sessionId = <replace-with-actual-session-id>
GET {{baseUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}

### List Artifacts in Session
GET {{baseUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/artifacts

### Update Session Status (Close Session)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "closed"
}

### Join Session as Participant
POST {{baseUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/participants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participant_ref": "anonymous"
}

### Create Session Event (play)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participant_ref": "anonymous",
  "event_type": "play",
  "video_time_seconds": 120,
  "payload": {}
}

### Create Session Event (seek)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participant_ref": "anonymous",
  "event_type": "seek",
  "video_time_seconds": 300,
  "payload": {}
}

### Ask Question in Session
POST {{baseUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/questions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question_text": "What was discussed at the 5-minute mark?"
}

### Ask Question in Session with Video Timestamp
POST {{baseUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/questions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question_text": "What was discussed at the 5-minute mark?",
  "video_time_seconds": 300
}

### Ask Question with Video Timestamp (Artifact-scoped)
POST {{baseUrl}}/artifacts/{{artifactId}}/questions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question_text": "What is the main topic?",
  "video_time_seconds": 120
}

### Get Session Questions (recent, reverse chronological)
GET {{baseUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/questions

### Get Session Timeline (chronological order for replay)
GET {{baseUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/timeline

### Get Session Timeline with Limit
GET {{baseUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/timeline?limit=50
